+## Independent verification (from scratch, disjoint from reporter code)
+
+Scratch: `/tmp/opencode/exec_p1_front_verify_20261122.py`, `exec_p1_n7_tight_20261122.py`,
+`exec_p1_n5_tight.py`, `exec_p1_n6_tight.py`; result logs `p1_n7_tight_out.txt`.
+
+My implementation uses a different canonical form (colour refinement by in/out-degree
+and sorted neighbour colours, lexicographic minimum over within-class permutations)
+and a memoized tight-strategy-existence DFS with the information lower bound
+ceil(log2 e(P)): exhibiting a height-lb strategy gives m<=lb, the counting bound gives
+m>=lb, hence m=lb exactly. I did not use the reporter's iso+dual quotient or their
+plain labelled DP.
+
+| n | F(P_1), my value | free-free value | endpoint-free value | gap | reporter |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| <=4 | orbits tie (endpoint attains F) | — | — | 0 | tie |
+| 5 | 6 | 6 | 1+max(6,5)=7 | +1 | 6/6/7 |
+| 6 | 9 | 9 | 1+max(8,7), lb-8 child NOT tight -> 10 | +1 | 9/9/10 |
+| 7 | 12 = S(7)-1 | 12 (children (11,11) tight) | 12 (children (11,10) tight) | 0 | 12/12/12 |
+
+At n=7 all 10 endpoint-free pairs and all 10 free-free pairs attain F(P_1)=12; so both
+orbits are optimal and the forced-free-pair invariant is unsound. The method
+cross-validates: it gives endpoint gap +1 at n=5,6 and gap 0 at n=7, so it discriminates
+rather than forcing the pattern. Three independent implementations (reporter quotient
+DP, reporter plain DP, my canonical tight search) agree at n=7.
+
+VERDICT: ACCEPT the refutation at n=7 as independently confirmed.
